Annotations: |
  This cell is the public presentation surface of the Quick Answers feature (voice-driven
  search-and-summarize): one presentable view controller, the navigation callback its host must
  implement, and the telemetry callback set it must implement. The speech-capture and
  results-fetch backend behind it (recording engines, transcription, the results service) is a
  separate, internal implementation detail of this same target and is out of scope for this
  cell — this cell documents only what a screen embedding Quick Answers actually depends on.

---

"QuickAnswersViewController()":
  location: QuickAnswersViewController.swift
  annotations: |
    Presents the Quick Answers modal: a voice-recording UI that transcribes speech, searches for
    an answer, and displays the result with its sources.

    Constructed with a navigation handler, a presentation transition style, user preferences,
    the presenting window's UUID, a theme manager, a telemetry sink, a config fetcher, and an
    optional "learn more" URL.
  properties:
    "themeManager -> ThemeManager": |
      Theme manager consulted for the current color theme.
    "currentWindowUUID -> WindowUUID?": |
      UUID of the window this controller is presented in (multi-window iPad support).
  methods:
    "viewDidLoad()": |
      Builds the view hierarchy, applies the current theme, and registers view-model callbacks.
    "viewWillAppear(animated: Bool)": |
      Starts the Quick Answers flow (opt-in check, then recording) the first time the view
      appears.
    "presentationControllerDidDismiss(controller: UIPresentationController)": |
      Treats an interactive sheet dismissal the same as tapping the close button.
    "applyTheme()": |
      Re-applies the current theme's colors to every subview.

"QuickAnswersNavigationHandler()":
  location: QuickAnswersNavigationHandler.swift
  annotations: |
    Implemented by whatever presents `QuickAnswersViewController`, to receive the outcome when
    the user dismisses it.
  methods:
    "dismissQuickAnswers(with navigationType: QuickAnswersNavigationType?)": |
      Called when the user dismisses the Quick Answers screen.

      `navigationType`: the follow-up navigation to perform (open a URL, or run a search with a
      given query string), or nil if the user dismissed without choosing an action. The two
      possible cases wrap either a URL to open or a search query string.

"QuickAnswersTelemetry()":
  location: QuickAnswersTelemetry.swift
  annotations: |
    Implemented by the app to record Quick Answers usage events; `QuickAnswersViewController`
    and its view model call these at each stage of the flow.
  methods:
    "quickAnswersRequested()": |
      The user initiated the Quick Answers flow.
    "recordingStarted()": |
      Voice capture began.
    "recordingCompleted(outcome: Bool, errorType: String?)": |
      Transcription finished.

      `outcome`: whether transcription succeeded
      `errorType`: description of the failure when `outcome` is false
    "resultsStarted()": |
      The results backend started fetching an answer for the transcribed text.
    "resultsCompleted(outcome: Bool, errorType: String?)": |
      The results backend finished fetching an answer.

      `outcome`: whether the fetch succeeded
      `errorType`: description of the failure when `outcome` is false
    "citationTapped()": |
      The user tapped a citation/source link in the results.
    "closed()": |
      The Quick Answers screen was dismissed.
    "consentShown(agreed: Bool)": |
      The opt-in consent dialogue was shown and resolved.

      `agreed`: whether the user accepted

